Open Wayle's native network manager from the dashboard Wi-Fi tile and add QR sharing.

A primary click now navigates to the existing Wayle network dropdown content,
so scanning, saved-profile activation, password entry, disconnect and forget
all remain native. A secondary click preserves the quick radio toggle.

The connected Wi-Fi card can render an inline QR code. Secrets are requested
from NetworkManager only when the user presses QR, the Wi-Fi payload is piped
to qrencode over stdin, and no password is placed in argv or a temporary file.
Open, WEP and personal WPA profiles are supported; Enterprise and OWE profiles
return a clear unsupported message.

